    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4614356/Central-College/Student-CAB-Generalist": {
      "title": "Student CAB Generalist",
      "description": "Central College - Student CAB Generalist In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Student CAB Generalist Central College Apply Student CAB Generalist PELLA, IA Apply Job Type Part-time Description About CAB The Campus Activities Board consists of a small, cohesive, and enthusiastic staff of event leaders who oversee various aspects of campus programming. CAB’s overall purpose is to develop programs and initiatives which support the Integrated Learning outcome goals at Central College and reflect the values of Central College’s Welcome Statement Each member of the board can lead events as well as serve on event planning teams to support other board members’ events All members will develop and enhance event planning and management skills communication skills interpersonal relationships with peers and professional staff through regular training and practical experience Who is eligible? Any Central College student who will be studying on campus for the Fall semester and enrolled full-time with 12 or more credit hours is eligible to apply Seniors who have not previously served on CAB must have previous program planning experience Strong academic achievement for consideration All applicants must have a minimum GPA of 2.5 to apply. Requirements What is the time commitment? attend bi-weekly meetings (2-3 hours per month) fulfill office hour obligations (2 hours per week) complete additional event leader responsibilities time commitment per week may vary depending upon the event schedule meetings office hours other CAB related initiatives weeks with multiple events are often busier than others, (i.e., Homecoming, Final Fling, training and retreat) most of the time commitment is spent setting up for, running, and cleaning up after events. creating and maintaining publicity and other event marketing projects. maintaining professional, business-oriented relationships with agencies artists while making the necessary arrangements to bring activities to campus. using and assisting others with the basic set-up and operation of the campus sound and audio/visual equipment researching presenting organizing new campus activities related to the events of the current and/or upcoming semester. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy"
    },
